// #taxon[Taxon]
#title[Cartesian Decomposition of fixed shape]
Recall the definition of the cartesian decomposition
#embed("00DQ")[]

#embed("00E7")[]

$
  S_n ~= (("Fin"_n, [n]) = ("Fin"_n, [n])
$

We can view the $S_n$ as
$
  S_n := (S ~= S)
$

write $(A,B,e) : "cart-dec"_(k,l)(S)$ for $(A,B,p_1,p_2,e)$.

Now the $S_n$ acts on $"cart-dec"_(k,l)(S)$ by
$
  sigma * (A,B,e) := (A,B, sigma @ e)
$

Transitivity (there is only one orbit)

Consider two decompositions
$
  (A,B,e), (A',B',e') : "cart-dec"_(k,l)(S)
$
